# Stub inventory for the `openbao_init_unseal` role's offline syntax-check /
# wiring smoke test (spec fix-openbao-sysctl-posix-collection, task 5 / C3;
# design C3).
#
# This inventory exists ONLY to give `ansible-playbook --syntax-check` a target
# to bind the role against — it performs NO host mutation. It points at the
# loopback host with a local connection so no SSH, no remote host, and no real
# infrastructure is ever touched. The conventional Ansible role `tests/` layout
# (tests/inventory + tests/test.yml + tests/ansible.cfg) is used, mirroring
# ansible/roles/common/tests/inventory.
#
# `--syntax-check` is the HARD GATE for this role: it resolves every bound
# module (including `ansible.posix.sysctl`, the module whose wrong-collection
# FQCN this fix corrects) against the pinned + installed collections without
# touching a host. A `--check` run against this local host, by contrast, may
# surface ENVIRONMENTAL errors rather than role defects — this role does live
# `docker exec` against a running OpenBao container, `uri` calls to a live
# OpenBao API, and a live `sysctl` write, none of which exist on the authoring
# host (which runs no OpenBao), and the role's full run MUTATES. So `--check` is
# best-effort wiring confirmation only; `--syntax-check` is the real gate.
localhost ansible_connection=local
